From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:34:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rstrtmgr: Implement the Restart Manager.

Sessions are kept in HKCU\Software\Microsoft\RestartManager\SessionNNNN, as Windows keeps them, so another process
joins one by its key.  RmGetList finds the processes using the registered files through
FileProcessIdsUsingFileInformation, the registered processes by their start time and the registered services
through the service manager, and tells whether each can be restarted from its RegisterApplicationRestart
registration.  RmShutdown asks applications to close with WM_QUERYENDSESSION and WM_ENDSESSION with
ENDSESSION_CLOSEAPP, hidden windows included, stops services, and with RmForceShutdown terminates what does not
go; RmRestart starts them again with their registered command lines.  Filters, RmJoinSession and
RmCancelCurrentTask are implemented as well.

The results match Windows 11 build 29671: a console application is RmConsole and named after its image without
version information, ERROR_BAD_ARGUMENTS comes back for a count with no array, an application that did not close
leaves ERROR_FAIL_SHUTDOWN with RmStatusRunning | RmStatusErrorOnStop, and one restarted runs again
(RmStatusRunning | RmStatusStopped | RmStatusRestarted) until the new process ends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

